All six features are implemented and passing end-to-end tests. Here's what was changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now validates the `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS` and raises HTTP 401 if missing or invalid; returns the username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Four changes to existing/additional endpoints:

1. **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` query params for filtering, plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20) for pagination. Filters are combinable; pagination slices the filtered result.

2. **`POST /tasks`** (status 201) — Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` against the projects list (404 if not found). Auto-generates a unique integer ID. Returns the created task.

3. **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Applies partial updates (only fields set in the `TaskUpdate` body). Returns 404 if the task doesn't exist.

4. **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Removes and returns the task. Returns 404 if not found.
